This directory is dedicated for user-supplied scripts/executables.
vifm modifies its PATH environment variable to let user run those
scripts without specifying full path.  All subdirectories are added
as well.  File in a subdirectory overrules file with the same name
in parent directories.  Restart might be needed to recognize files
in newly created or renamed subdirectories.
Asynchronous previews
---------------------
vifmrc sets previewprg to vifm-preview for every file type. The foreground
command only starts a worker or displays its result; file reads, MIME detection,
archive listing and thumbnail conversion run outside vifm. A loading message
remains until the worker asks this vifm instance to redraw via its server name.
The 90 MiB input limit is retained; converter runtime is limited to 45 seconds,
text output to 128 KiB, and directory listings to 256 entries.

Each request owns a private temporary directory and process group. Navigation
cancels unfinished requests, kills converters and their descendants, then removes
all request files. Completed output survives redraws and is removed on the next
selection or when vifmrun exits. No incomplete thumbnails enter a shared cache.
vifmrun isolates sessions, closes workers on exit, and keeps FIFO operations
nonblocking. A watchdog cleans up workers if vifm exits unexpectedly or was
launched directly. Client-server support is required for automatic refresh.

Static images use ueberzug; GIF/WebP and short video animations use kitten icat
when a terminal is available. Missing converters produce an unavailable message.
Existing fileviewer commands can still invoke the vifmimg compatibility wrapper.

Run regression checks with:
    python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v
